From 914c93394f52c24c16bba6a91accc9b46a563da1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:46:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Anchor the end-to-end fixtures to the real clock so the
 suite stops decaying
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The unit checks freeze time at NOW and hand that same instant to the
classifier, so they cannot drift. The end-to-end check cannot do that: it
runs the engine as a subprocess, and the engine reads Date.now(). Fixture
dates built from the frozen NOW therefore aged one day per real day.

The suite was already red. The lead written as "at risk" — last called 11
days before the frozen NOW — was 14 days old by the time the engine looked
at it, past Warm Back Up's 13-day neglect line, so "1 at risk, 2 neglected"
had become "0 at risk, 3 neglected". Nobody changed anything; the calendar
did it.

A decaying test is worse than a missing one. It fails on a day unrelated to
the change in front of you, which trains everyone to read a red suite as
noise — and this is the suite standing between a bug and an engine that
reassigns real leads away from real agents.

battr:test: 134 checks, green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
