From 54bb1b7d3fce524fdfabcc6ed907fcc37df925a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:56:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Say plainly in the report that the owner-group
 exclusion protects nobody
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rules.excludeOwnerGroupIds is [52555] — "Battr Paused" in the live Battr
config. The condition reads owner_group_ids, normalized from
assignedUserGroupIds / groupIds on the FUB person, and inspect-fub-fields
confirmed against the live account that Follow Up Boss returns neither.
Every contact carries an empty array, so "not in group 52555" is true for
everyone and the rule excludes nobody.

The rule not working is not the problem. The problem is that it reads as
though it does. Someone puts an agent into the Battr Paused group in FUB,
reasonably expects their leads to stop being swept, and nothing about the
config or the run says otherwise — their leads get swept anyway.

There was already a warning, but only on stderr, in a CI log nobody opens.
It now appears in the report itself, above the counts, and it names the
exemption that does work (exemptAgents, by assigned-agent name) along with
who is currently on it.

The rule is left in place rather than deleted: it documents what the live
Battr config does, and deleting it would erase the only record of why anyone
knows this. Emptying the array silences the block.

Mike Roland stays protected either way — he is in exemptAgents by name, and
the sweep loop checks that a second time independently of classification.

