From 8adbf2c756811fa5ae3a5e4150d74ababf960506 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Match nurture timeframes by FUB's id as well as its
 name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The four nurture lists select leads by timeframe. They currently match on the
timeframe NAME — and Follow Up Boss's API does not return a name.
inspect-fub-fields confirmed it against the live account: `timeframe` is
absent from the person payload, `timeframeId` is present.

So all four lists match nobody. Nothing errors, because an empty list is not
an error, and roughly 1,262 leads Battr audits are invisible to this engine.

Matching by id is also the faithful copy. Battr's own rules address
timeframes and stages by numeric id (crm_stage_exid IS ANY OF [98,2,99,10,8]);
matching on the name was a stopgap from when the id map was unavailable.

Membership is now two OR'd groups — name, or id — because which one is
readable depends on the account: the name is what a CSV export carries, the
id is what the API returns. Either alone is a silent single point of failure.

TIMEFRAME_IDS ships EMPTY, and `IS ANY OF []` matches nothing, so this commit
changes no behavior on its own. Filling it in widens the sweep population,
since those four lists feed ⭐️ Team Leads — that is a deliberate act with a
before-and-after dry run, not a side effect of a refactor.

Two supporting fixes:

  - List 1145 ("Nurtures No Timeframe") now requires BOTH the name and the id
    to be blank. Requiring only the name meant every lead whose timeframe we
    merely cannot READ landed in the has-no-timeframe bucket — which is the
    account's exact state today, and would have made that list look like the
    whole nurture database.
  - normalizeContact separates the two conditions that used to look alike:
    `timeframeUnresolved` (no timeframe at all — a data gap, list 1145's job)
    and `timeframeIdOnly` (has one, we cannot read it — a translation gap,
    fixed by filling in the map). They want opposite responses.

To get the map, either route settles it without guessing: census now prints
timeframe id → contact count database-wide, and inspect probes for a
timeframes endpoint and for a timeframe custom field. Failing both, FUB's
People screen exports Timeframe by name and the two join on FUB ID.

The audit warns on stderr and in the report when leads carry an id with the
map unfilled, listing the ids and their counts.

battr:test: 169 checks, including one that patches a copy of list 1106 to
prove the id branch works end to end, and one asserting the shipped map is
still empty so nothing widens by accident.

