From 62e661ca2d58437ed6b5efe61aa276d5ebdf4b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 23:44:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Stop the first run inventing 53,786 at bats, and stop
 the header misreporting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both found in the first real audit against Follow Up Boss (run 2026-09-04-e1vs).

THE AT BATS LEDGER WAS FABRICATED. Detection diffs ownership against the
previous run's snapshot. On the first run there is no snapshot, so every
contact read as "never seen, owned now" — a brand new lead. The run wrote
53,786 events, every one typed brand_new_lead, every one stamped the same
instant, and the scoreboard credited one agent with 29,195 at bats in 180 days
at 100% retention with 0 pond claims.

That is worse than an obvious error. A conversion rate computed over a
fabricated denominator still renders as a tidy percentage and reads as fact —
16.6% next to a name, in a table headed "last 180 days", on a scoreboard about
people's performance. The first run now records the snapshot and claims
nothing; at bats accrue from the second run onward, which is what the ledger
was always documented to mean. Real history comes from a Battr At Bats export
instead, and has to be captured before the subscription lapses.

THE HEADER REPORTED THRESHOLDS THAT WERE NOT USED. It printed "thresholds: at
risk 7d, neglected 14d" on every run. Those are the SIMPLE-mode globals;
nothing in list mode consults them. Every list carries its own — 2/4 days on
Hot Leads through 93/96 on Quarterly Nurture. Anyone reading the report was
told the engine ran on 7/14. It did not.

The same line called the raw Follow Up Boss pull "leads audited" — 53,786, next
to a summary totalling a few hundred, which invites exactly the wrong
conclusion about which number reconciles against Battr's 865. It now names both
and marks which one is the audited population.

The existing at-bats checks passed an empty snapshot as a shorthand for "new
lead"; they now start from an established baseline, the way every night after
the first one does.

battr:test: 184 checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BY8icdQLaS9G2YxbAmEBDv
